Bootstrap: docker
From: condaforge/miniforge3:24.3.0-0

%labels
    Maintainer sdweave2@ncsu.edu
    Source https://github.com/schneebergerlab/syri
    Version 1.8.2

%help
    syri — identifies synteny and structural rearrangements between two chromosome-level assemblies, bundled with MUMmer4.

    Why this image exists: the stock biocontainer
    (quay.io/biocontainers/syri:1.8.2--py310h0c14f88_0) does not ship
    MUMmer, but syri shells out to MUMmer's `show-snps` (`-s`, default
    "show-snps" on PATH) to call SNPs/indels whenever it is given nucmer
    output (-c <coords> -d <delta>) without --cigar. That run fails with
    "Error in finding SNPs using show-snps". This image adds mummer4 to the
    same environment so nucmer/delta-filter/show-coords/show-snps are all
    on PATH alongside syri. It also adds MUMmer's optional plotting
    utilities (gnuplot, fig2dev, xfig) so mummerplot works.

    Version note: same syri build (bioconda 1.8.2 py310h0c14f88_0) and the
    same pinned Python stack as the stock biocontainer it replaced in place
    as the syri/1.8.2 module. The only differences are the added mummer4
    and the OS-level plotting utilities (gnuplot, fig2dev, xfig from apt).

    Usage:
        apptainer run syri-1.8.2.sif -c <coords|sam|bam|paf> -r ref.fa -q qry.fa [options]

    Key options (full list: apptainer run syri-1.8.2.sif --help):
        -c FILE         Alignment input (nucmer .coords table, SAM, BAM, or PAF)
        -r FILE         Reference genome FASTA
        -q FILE         Query genome FASTA
        -d FILE         nucmer .delta file (required with -F T and no --cigar)
        -F {T,S,B,P}    Input format: T=table/coords (default), S=SAM, B=BAM, P=PAF
        --dir DIR       Output directory
        --prefix STR    Prefix for output files
        --nc INT        Number of cores
        -k              Keep intermediate files
        --cigar         Get SNPs/indels from CIGAR strings instead of show-snps
        -s PATH         show-snps executable (default: show-snps, provided here)
        --nosnp         Skip SNP/indel calling
        --novcf         Do not combine all outputs into one VCF file
        --samplename S  Sample name used in the output VCF
        --no-chrmatch   Do not auto-match chromosome IDs between genomes

    Bundled MUMmer4 programs (use with `apptainer exec`):
        nucmer, delta-filter, show-coords, show-snps, mummer, dnadiff,
        mummerplot

    Plotting utilities (MUMmer's optional deps, Ubuntu 20.04 apt builds):
        gnuplot (gnuplot-x11; png/postscript/x11 terminals), fig2dev, xfig
        mummerplot --png / --postscript work headless; the interactive x11
        terminal and xfig need X11 forwarding (ssh -X).

    Example (nucmer workflow, everything inside this one container):
        apptainer exec syri-1.8.2.sif nucmer --maxmatch -c 100 -b 500 -l 50 -t 8 ref.fa qry.fa -p out
        apptainer exec syri-1.8.2.sif delta-filter -m -i 90 -l 100 out.delta > out.filtered.delta
        apptainer exec syri-1.8.2.sif show-coords -THrd out.filtered.delta > out.filtered.coords
        apptainer run  syri-1.8.2.sif -c out.filtered.coords -d out.filtered.delta -r ref.fa -q qry.fa

%post -c /bin/bash
    set -e
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # Hazel bind-mount points
    mkdir -p /rs1 /share /home /usr/local/usrapps

    # MUMmer's optional plotting utilities (README minimums: gnuplot 4.0,
    # fig2dev 3.2.3, xfig 3.2). Installed from apt, not conda: fig2dev and
    # xfig aren't on conda-forge, and keeping gnuplot out of the conda solve
    # leaves the pinned syri stack below untouched. mummerplot finds gnuplot
    # on PATH (/usr/bin). gnuplot-x11 = png/postscript + x11 terminals,
    # without pulling in Qt.
    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends gnuplot-x11 fig2dev xfig
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # Pattern 4 (bioconda via miniforge3 + mamba — see CLAUDE.md lessons 2,
    # 6, 7). No GPU-capable dependencies, so no GPU addendum applies.
    #
    # Runtime stack pinned to exactly match the stock biocontainer this image
    # replaces (quay.io/biocontainers/syri:1.8.2--py310h0c14f88_0), so the
    # only intended difference is the added mummer4. Unpinned, the solve
    # drifted to python 3.11 / pandas 3.1.1 / numpy 2.4.6 / scipy 1.17.1 —
    # pandas 3 is a breaking major release (same reason vcontact3 pins a
    # pandas-2 stack). syri is pinned to the biocontainer's exact build string.
    mamba create -n syri -y -c conda-forge -c bioconda \
        "syri=1.8.2=py310h0c14f88_0" \
        mummer4=4.0.1 \
        python=3.10.20 \
        pandas=2.3.3 \
        numpy=2.2.6 \
        scipy=1.15.2 \
        pysam=0.24.0
    mamba clean -afy

%environment
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    export PATH="/opt/conda/envs/syri/bin:$PATH"

%runscript
    exec syri "$@"

%test
    # Multi-command test: set -e so a failing `syri --help` can't be masked
    # by a later passing line.
    set -e
    # %environment is not sourced for %test (see EDTA's def) — set PATH here.
    export PATH="/opt/conda/envs/syri/bin:$PATH"
    syri --help
    # The whole point of this image: syri's default `-s show-snps` must
    # resolve, along with the rest of the nucmer toolchain.
    for prog in show-snps nucmer delta-filter show-coords mummerplot gnuplot fig2dev xfig; do
        command -v "$prog" || { echo "ERROR: $prog not on PATH" >&2; exit 1; }
    done
    nucmer --version
    gnuplot --version
    fig2dev -V
